((date 2026-10-13) (slug short-setup-map)
 (hypothesis
  "Short setup map (pre-registration dev/plans/short-setup-map-2026-10-12.md, #3274, confirmed by the user; amendment 1 #3278 dividend splits): does the book's short setup show an edge? Population: every Stage 3 -> 4 weekly transition (stage_chart default classifier, adjusted closes) of a PIT top-3000 v12 list member, breakdowns 2000-01-07 -> 2025-12-26, close >= $5 (sensitivity $17), one event per symbol per 26 weeks. Entries E1 next close after the breakdown, E2 first weekly close in weeks +1..+8 at or above the broken support. Outcomes O1 no stop at +20/60/120 bars, O2 buy-stop 1 % above the Stage-3 high held to +120 bars; excess vs an SPY short, total return. Primary cells P1 (E1) and P2 (E2) = SPY early Stage 4 or Stage 3, advance >= 30 %, RS not rising, sector weak. Edge on O2 = n >= 100, mean >= +2 %, median > 0, beat >= 55 %, halves agree, O1 +60 agrees. Proxy screen: may conclude only build or no-build.")
 (base_scenario
  "short-setup-map-2026-10-12: offline event screen, host awk over .sweep-output/short-setup-map/stages/ (stage_chart replay of 9,222 symbols) and data/ bars + dividends; SPY weekly stage from index-hedge-screen-2026-10-12/results/spy-weekly-stage.csv; 45,599 events in results/events/<year>.csv; scripts/run.sh regenerates")
 (window_id top3000-pitv12-2000-2025-stage34-breakdown-events) (baseline_label spy-short)
 (variants
  (((label P1-E1-O2) (config_hash short-setup-P1) (aggregate ()))
   ((label P2-E2-O2) (config_hash short-setup-P2) (aggregate ()))))
 (verdict Reject)
 (notes
  "NO-BUILD DECISION (proxy screen; nothing was built, no flag to retire; does not license 'shorts cannot work'). P1 n=4,235 mean -2.44 % median -3.76 % beat 29.7 %; P2 n=3,530 mean -0.85 % median -1.91 % beat 31.4 %; both fail criteria 2-4 by wide margins ($17 floor: P1 beat 29.2 %, P2 31.4 %); no descriptive cell clears the >= 58 % bar. WHY: (1) selection - without a stop the 45,599 breakdowns are a coin flip vs an SPY short (+60 bars beat 51.4 %, median +0.49 %); each checklist item given the others selects worse shorts; (2) market timing - SPY early Stage 4 is the worst slice, SPY rose 6.3 % on average over P1 holds, broken names rebound with the index; (3) the stop (Stage-3 sliver of 1-2 weeks -> median room 10 %) turns the coin flip into a loser, but P1 drifts negative without any stop, so no stop width rescues it; (4) E2 is mostly a one-week shift (48 % of events never close below the broken support). Dividends: payers are not worse shorts (O2 beat 34.2 % both); the bigdiv-in-hold split is look-ahead biased (defect 8), decision-time split (results/analysis/divsplit.txt) 1,093 events beat 29.5 % mean -2.73 % vs 34.3 % / -1.24 %: a known large dividend makes a slightly worse short. Two independent results-analyst reads agree. NOTHING WAS BUILT, SO NOTHING RETIRES: the existing short flags stay default-off axes until the user decides whether to close the track. RECOMMENDATION (user decides): close single-name shorts as a strategy track; remaining untested book levers: short interest (data-blocked) and a price-defined wide top (second read: one cheap pre-registered screen, expected to fail). DEFECTS: AKR raw sentinel 999999.9999; BCE 2000-05 uncredited Nortel distribution (#3215 class); vendor splices (#3239 class, BELM -47,833 %); data/sectors.csv survivor-only (91 % of no-sector events delisted); bigdiv look-ahead; advance low may follow the high; WTR zero bars. Writeup dev/experiments/short-setup-map-2026-10-12/README.md."))
